        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la contravention",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la contravention — \"the fine (for a driving offence), the ticket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Il a reçu une contravention pour excès de vitesse. He got a ticket for speeding."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Informally un PV, short for procès-verbal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "contravention is a learned formation on Late Latin contrāvenīre 'to oppose, to go against', from contrā 'against' and venīre 'to come' (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
